{title: At the Foot of the Cross (Ashes to Beauty)}
{key: E}

{comment: Verse 1}
[B]At the foot [C#m]of the cross
[A]Where grace and [E]suffering meet
[B]You have [C#m]shown me Your love
[A]Through the [B]judgment You received
And [F#m]You've [E/G#]won  [A]my  [B]heart
And [F#m]You've [E/G#]won  [A]my  [A2/B]heart      Now I Can

{comment: Chorus}
[E]Trade [B]these [F#m]ashes in [E]for beauty
[E]And [B]wear [F#m]forgiveness like a crown
[E]Coming [B]to kiss the [F#m]feet of mercy
I lay [C#m]every [B]bur[F#m]den down
At [B]the foot [E]of the cross

{comment: Verse 2}
[B]At the foot [C#m]of the cross
[A]Where I am [E]made complete
[B]You have [C#m]given me life
[A]Through the death [B]You bore for me
And [F#m]You've [E/G#]won  [A]my  [B]heart
And [F#m]You've [E/G#]won  [A]my  [A2/B]heart      Now I Can
